 Setup needs an existing Node.js 24.12+ and Python 3.11+ interpreter; it uses only Python's standard-library TOML parser. Opus execution also needs an installed, authenticated Claude Code CLI. Setup checks its existing path, version, and options; runs reuse its existing authentication. It does not install Claude Code or rewrite its global settings. Codex presents setup onboarding after installation. Setup registers the two bundled custom-agent definitions and their native config references, plus a description-only `pstack-general-purpose` role that leaves your existing default role intact. It stores your role choices in `$CODEX_HOME/pstack-for-codex/models.json`, defaulting to `~/.codex`. Re-run setup after an update or a prior-version restore to synchronize its owned agent files. Existing user edits stop replacement; role preferences are retained.
 
 Before restoring an older all-Sol bundle, use the current setup to explicitly save Codex-only role choices. Preferences with a Claude executor use schema 2; older helpers reject that format and leave the file intact. Native-only preferences use schema 1, which those older bundles can read.
 
-Before removing the plugin, ask setup to unregister its managed agents. It removes only its unchanged agent files and owned role declarations; unrelated configuration and your model preferences remain. Then use `codex plugin remove pstack-for-codex@pstack-for-codex-local`. Native plugin removal does not run an agent-cleanup hook.
+Before removing the plugin, ask setup to unregister its managed agents. It removes only its unchanged agent files and owned role declarations; unrelated configuration and your model preferences remain. Then use `codex plugin remove pstack-for-codex@pstack-for-codex`. Native plugin removal does not run an agent-cleanup hook.
 
